<!--
    Perplexity iOS 26.46.0, DeviceKit (arm64 Mach-O, stripped):
    `swift56override_swift_task_create_common` is

        cmp  x5, #0x20
        mov  w8, #0x20
        csel x5, x5, x8, hi
        br   x6

    and kuna printed `(*a6)(); // jump-as-call` with the clamp gone: the call
    took no arguments, so the `csel` had no reader and dead-code removal took
    it.  Every Swift async `resume_parent` continuation and every vtable or
    witness tail dispatch in the app had the same empty call.

    Root cause (P4, active-input trial scoring).  The function never writes
    x0..x4, so heritage names them nowhere and the call gets no trial for them;
    buildTrialMap synthesizes an UNREFERENCED trial per slot, scored inactive.
    ParamListStandard::forceInactiveChain (fspec.cc:1519, maxchain 2) reads a
    run of more than two inactive slots as the end of the argument list and
    demotes every later trial, the actively written x5 included.  The same
    shape with three arguments, a run of two, recovered all three: the hole
    was filled below the active trial.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring", option `passthrough`
    (kuna_passthrough.rs, default on).  At a CALL SITE a REGISTER the function
    hands on untouched (unreferenced, or the function's own input Varnode in
    place) counts toward neither the run nor its end; the tail loop that
    fills the holes below the last active trial takes it.  Off reproduces the
    empty call.

    The fixture is the construct re-assembled from `void f(long a,long b,long
    c,long d,void (*fp)(long,long,long,long)) { if (d<=32) d=32; fp(a,b,c,d); }`
    at clang -O2 (f4: `csel x3; br x4`), the same with a statement after the
    call so the dispatch is a `blr` (m5, five arguments), the three-argument
    shape that always recovered (f3, a run of two), and `k(a,b,fp){ fp(a+1,b); }`
    (k: `add x0; br x2`), whose forwarded x1 stands AFTER the last active
    register and must stay dropped in both passes.

    i9 is the shape gcc's IPA register allocation leaves at a call to a local
    function it knows clobbers nothing: `ldr x3, [x9]; bl g1` with x0..x2 the
    function's own parameters, all four read after the call.  g1 is `ret`,
    a callee that takes no register, so x3 is not an argument the forwarded
    registers lead up to and the call stays `g1()` in both passes (the
    unguarded rule printed `g1(a0,a1,a2,dat_2000)`).
-->
